============================================================\
ENCAPSULATION \'97 HOW DATA ACTUALLY MOVES\
[DURING VIDEO]\
============================================================\
\
Encapsulation = as data moves [       data             ] the stack, each layer\
wraps it with a [       header             ] containing the info that layer needs.\
\
Layer 2 also adds a [        trailer            ] at the end \'97 used to check for\
[          transmission          ] errors on the receiving end.\
\
The Physical layer transmits the result as [         bits           ] over the medium.\
\
Decapsulation = the receiving device removes headers layer by layer,\
moving [          up          ] the stack, until the data reaches the application.\
\
------------------------------------------------------------\
PDU NAMES \'97 WHAT THE DATA IS CALLED AT EACH LAYER\
[DURING VIDEO]\
------------------------------------------------------------\
\
These terms show up in AWS logs, tcpdump output, and documentation constantly.\
\
Layer 4 using TCP  \uc0\u8594   [       segment             ]\
Layer 4 using UDP  \uc0\u8594   [           datagram         ]\
Layer 3            \uc0\u8594   [          packet          ]   \u8592  most common term in networking\
Layer 2            \uc0\u8594   [         frame           ]   \u8592  what physically travels over the wire\
\
The contents inside any PDU (not including that layer's own header) = the\
[           payload         ]\
\
\
