============================================================\
HOW LAYERS SEPARATE \'97 WHY THIS MATTERS FOR DEVOPS\
[DURING VIDEO]\
============================================================\
\
Because layers are modular, you can swap a protocol at one layer without\
changing the [        other            ].\
\
Jeremy gives two examples \'97 write them here:\
\
Example 1: swap [          HTTP          ] for TFTP over UDP\
           \'97 lower layers don't care what the upper layers are doing\
\
Example 2: swap wired [          ethernet          ] for wireless Wi-Fi\
           \'97 upper layers don't care how the signal gets there\
\
\
[AFTER VIDEO \'97 DEVOPS BRIDGE]\
\
This separation is why DevOps tooling is composable. Answer these:   \
\
Why can you put Nginx in front of any backend app regardless of what language it's written in?\
Because nginx operates at layer 7 the application layer specifically for http portal. It doesn\'92t care if the payload inside that https request was generated by python.\
Why can Docker swap its network driver (bridge, host, overlay) without breaking your app?\
The container sees a standard virtual interface docker handles the translation to physical network at layer 2 and layer 3\
\
Why does moving your app from EC2 to Lambda not require rewriting how HTTP works?\
Both ec2 and lambda adhere to the same World Wide Web standards\
\
